From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: durunduk <drebdebian@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 04:10:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] tu: Wait for ME before BV vertex fetch after barriers on A8XX

tu_flush_for_stage() already emits CP_WAIT_FOR_ME right away on a8xx when
the destination stage is TU_STAGE_BV_CP (indirect parameters), because
a8xx dropped the implicit wait earlier GPUs had. The same is needed when
the destination is TU_STAGE_BV (vertex input, index fetch, pre-raster
shaders): the WFI alone does not stop BV from reading data written before
the barrier.

Seen on Styx: Blades of Greed (UE 5.6 through vkd3d-proton 0bb64c56,
Adreno 840, sysmem): the second level renders shattered geometry.
Bisected by adding flushes per barrier category (TU_FLUSH_HACK, 0009):

  CP_WAIT_FOR_ME at barriers with dst TU_STAGE_BV       clean
  CP_WAIT_MEM_WRITES at the same barriers               broken
  same waits with dst TU_STAGE_BV_CP or BR only         broken
  same waits at barriers outside a render pass only     clean
  same waits at barriers inside a render pass only      broken

CP_WAIT_FOR_ME only stalls the CP, so the cost is small.
---
diff --git a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
index ad3bd17..c0abc7f 100644
--- a/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
+++ b/src/freedreno/vulkan/tu_cmd_buffer.cc
@@ -6472,6 +6472,14 @@ tu_flush_for_stage(struct tu_cache_state *cache,
                cache->flush_bits |= TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_ME;
             else
                cache->pending_flush_bits |= TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_ME;
+         } else if (CHIP >= A8XX) {
+            /* On a8xx the WFI alone does not keep BV's vertex/index fetch
+             * from reading data written before the barrier either: UE5
+             * (vkd3d-proton) renders shattered geometry on Adreno 840 unless
+             * CP_WAIT_FOR_ME is emitted here too. CP_WAIT_MEM_WRITES did not
+             * help; CP_WAIT_FOR_ME alone did.
+             */
+            cache->flush_bits |= TU_CMD_FLAG_WAIT_FOR_ME;
          }
       } else {
          if (CHIP >= A7XX && by_region)
